# Static asset passthrough
/assets/* /assets/:splat 200

# Dynamic client-rendered app routes → app shell (200).
# Patterns are exact/placeholder-only and must NEVER overlap a prerendered
# static page: live-verified 2026-11-11 that a 200 rewrite beats the static
# file on Pages (the /calculators/* and /stories regressions). The shell target
# is "/" (the directory index): Pages' redirect validator IGNORES any
# splat rule pointing at /index.html as an "infinite loop", and a rewrite
# to a non-index .html file gets 308-redirected to its clean URL — both
# verified against wrangler's bundled pages-shared parser, 2026-10-27.
/rates/search              / 200
/rates/:category/in/:city  / 200
# /calculators/cd, /refinance, /affordability, /insurance rewrites REMOVED
# 2026-11-11: those routes have real prerendered snapshots (c0e9283) and a
# 200 rewrite wins over the static file on Pages, so the rules were serving
# the homepage shell on top of good static pages (live-verified).
/stories/:slug             / 200
/dashboard                 / 200
/dashboard/                / 200
/signup                    / 200
/signup/                   / 200
/ops                       / 200
/ops/                      / 200

# NO catch-all fallback. Pages' asset server serves /index.html with a
# 200 for unmatched paths ONLY while no 404.html exists; this project now
# ships a 404.html (emitted by scripts/prerender.mjs), so every unmatched
# path returns a genuine 404 with the site's NotFound page (soft-404 fix,
# 2026-10-27).
